    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d318">

                <pb facs="0261" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg211"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/306</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-14T18:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                                1917, 6 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>And Willard:</p>
                <p>Transport <hi rendition="#italic">Thomas</hi> arrived to-day. Conditions make it
                    absolutely imperative to delay decision as to landing for some days. It may be
                    necessary to sail quick. Cable instantly placing ship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thomas</hi> under my orders for any port in Japan we may select. Lose no
                    time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
